Let $s = a + b + c + d = 0.$  Then $a + b + c = -d,$ so
\[(a + b)(a + c)(b + c) = (a + b)(a + c)(-d) = -d(a + b)(a + c).\]Similarly,
\begin{align*}
(a + b)(a + d)(b + d) &= -c(a + b)(a + d), \\
(a + c)(a + d)(c + d) &= -b(a + c)(a + d), \\
(b + c)(b + d)(c + d) &= -a(b + c)(b + d).
\end{align*}Hence,
\begin{align*}
&|(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)(c + d)| \\
&= |abcd(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)| \\
&= |(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)|.
\end{align*}By AM-GM,
\begin{align*}
|(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)|^2 &= |a + b|^2 |a + c|^2 |a + d|^2 |b + c|^2 |b + d|^2 \\
&\le \left( \frac{|a + b|^2 + |a + c|^2 + |a + d|^2 + |b + c|^2 + |b + d|^2}{5} \right)^5.
\end{align*}Note that
\begin{align*}
|a + b|^2 &= (a + b)(\overline{a} + \overline{b}) \\
&= a \overline{a} + a \overline{b} + b \overline{a} + b \overline{b} \\
&= |a|^2 + a \overline{b} + b \overline{a} + |b|^2 \\
&= 2 + a \overline{b} + b \overline{a}.
\end{align*}Similarly,
\begin{align*}
|a + c|^2 &= 2 + a \overline{c} + c \overline{a}, \\
|a + d|^2 &= 2 + a \overline{d} + d \overline{a}, \\
|b + c|^2 &= 2 + b \overline{c} + c \overline{b}, \\
|b + d|^2 &= 2 + b \overline{d} + d \overline{b}.
\end{align*}Hence,
\[|a + b|^2 + |a + c|^2 + |a + d|^2 + |b + c|^2 + |b + d|^2 = 10 + (a + b + c + d)(\overline{a} + \overline{b} + \overline{c} + \overline{d}) = 10,\]so
\[|(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)|^2 \le 2^5 = 32.\]Hence,
\[|(a + b)(a + c)(a + d)(b + c)(b + d)(c + d)| \le \boxed{4 \sqrt{2}}.\]Equality occurs when $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d$ are equally spaced on the unit circle, as illustrated below.

